So, more to the point. The main NetHack interfaces I have been
playing, are ascii, ascii+color (local or nao), Qt tiles and more
recently Vulture's Eye. I've had fun with all, unspoiled and spoiled,
mostly dying (apart from an accident on nao). By the way, if you only
have fun in winning, NetHack might not be the game that suits you.

In my opinion, what differenciates Vulture's most is that the view is
centered on the hero, whereas in the other interfaces you see the
whole map from above. This has the effect that dark corridors feel a
lot more scarier and that you feel a lot more like in a maze (The
Mazes of Menace...). I personally like to switch between interfaces,
but Vulture's is definitely worth a try.

I think you know, but just to make sure, all NetHack interfaces may be
freely downloaded and distributed.

